WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.910
- So I want to take a second
and look at some egregious

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.858
but also unintentionally
hilarious police misconduct.

00:00:04.858 --> 00:00:07.220
(door slams)

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.933
All right, so the policeman
enters the garage,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.610
and then he just slams it into the car.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.163
Slams it again.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.270
Just...

00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:22.980
(host sighs deeply)

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.330
Yeah, it goes without saying,
this is entirely improper,

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.840
but I do want to highlight a
hilarious comment on Twitter

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.190
from Brian Hamilton who highlights

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.770
a kind of passive pro police speech

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.897
you often hear describing
conduct like this.

00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:35.100
"A car was damaged today

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.440
in an officer-involved door slamming.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.560
The car's manufacturer
says it was a good car

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.190
but the Carfax shows a
more complicated past."

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.330
Yeah, even when there's videos,

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.410
sometimes people have
to both sides things,

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.706
even when one of those
things is a car probably.

00:00:48.706 --> 00:00:49.583
(door slams)

